      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The quiet hum of the offseason in Toronto carries a different weight now, as the Maple Leafs - finished with a <strong>78-point, 8th-in-Atlantic</strong> campaign that ended too soon - pivot from regret to reconstruction. All eyes are on the top-six internal battle, where <strong>Easton Cowan, Gavin McKenna, and Jack Roslovic will fight for prime real estate</strong> alongside Auston Matthews. The rookie sensation, McKenna, the No. 1 pick in the 2026 Draft, has already signed his three-year entry-level deal and is tipped to match Matvei Michkov's debut-season impact, potentially filling Mitch Marner's void on the top line. Former netminder Jack Campbell's retirement adds a somber note to a roster reshaped by free agency, including the two-year, $4.25 million addition of Colton Sissons. The front office isn't dwelling on the past; it's building around youth and cap flexibility. <strong>What to watch: whether McKenna earns the top-line nod by camp's first puck drop.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 21, 2026"
      },
